  "id": "DrugBank_DB06768 - MONDO_4980",
  "verbalization": "Ammonium Lactate is associated with Atopic Eczema through a chain of indications that link it to dermatological conditions, specifically Dermatitis, Atopic. This relationship is supported by its use in treating Dermatitis, Atopic, which in turn is indicated for conditions like Crisaborole, Pimecrolimus, and Dupilumab, all of which are used in the management of Atopic Eczema. The shared indication of Dermatitis, Atopic across these pathways suggests a potential overlap in therapeutic mechanisms or pathophysiological processes. The evidence points to a possible role of Ammonium Lactate in the treatment of Atopic Eczema through its association with these medications, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader therapeutic context when evaluating the potential repurposing of Ammonium Lactate for Atopic Eczema.",
